abel":"2026 season stats","news":[{"headline":"Heisman race for Week 12: Wake Forest's Gio Lopez makes late push","description":"Much like his team, the Demon Deacons' QB has slipped under the radar much of the season -- but no more.","published":"2026-11-24T11:31:14.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50573849/heisman-race-wake-forest-gio-lopez","type":"Story","byline":"Bill Connelly","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Tiering the CFP favorites: Who's actually built to win on top of the odds board","description":"CFP futures got murkier after Saturday's results. But which teams can actually go far in the tournament?","published":"2026-11-24T12:03:22.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/betting/story/_/id/50573806/2026-college-football-playoff-cfp-futures-odds-picks","type":"Story","byline":"Pamela Maldonado","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Who's on the College Football Playoff bubble before committee's fourth ranking?","description":"A conference-by-conference look at which teams are contending for the playoff, who's close and who's out.","published":"2026-11-24T11:29:00.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50575185/cfp-playoff-2026-bubble-watch-week-fourth-ranking","type":"Story","byline":"Heather Dinich","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"What qualities make the perfect coach? We're borrowing from the best","description":"If we can build a coach in a lab, we can start with these qualities and skills.","published":"2026-11-24T11:23:43.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50476785/building-perfect-coach","type":"Story","byline":"Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"SEC to consider termination of LSU's membership at Dec. 3 meeting","description":"For the second time this year, the SEC is threatening to hold a vote of its chancellors and presidents on whether to kick LSU out of the league, according to a filing in federal court in Alabama on Monday.","published":"2026-11-24T02:55:51.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/mens-college-basketball/story/_/id/50577602/sec-consider-termination-lsu-membership","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Mark Schlabach","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Georgia defensive coordinator Glenn Schumann agrees to coach Florida State","description":"Georgia's Glenn Schumann, one of the country's top defensive coordinators and part of a staff that has the Bulldogs at No. 1 in the CFP rankings, agreed to a five-year deal to become the next coach at Florida State, the school announced Monday.","published":"2026-11-24T02:51:47.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50577665/uga-defensive-coordinator-schumann-coach-florida-state","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Andrea Adelson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Aiden Flora, nation's leading rusher, re-signs with Iowa State for next season","description":"Iowa State running back Aiden Flora, who leads the nation in rushing, announced Monday that he has re-signed with the Cyclones for next season.","published":"2026-11-23T23:57:14.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50577520/aiden-flora-nation-leading-rusher-re-signs-iowa-state","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"David Wilson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Texas A&M names John Thornton interim athletic director effective Dec. 1","description":"John Thornton will take over as interim athletic director at Texas A&M, effective Dec. 1, replacing the departed Trev Alberts.","published":"2026-11-23T22:07:34.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50576559/texas-names-john-thornton-interim-ad-effective-dec-1","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Sources: Giants DC Dennard Wilson interviews for HC job at alma mater Maryland","description":"Giants defensive coordinator Dennard Wilson had a virtual interview recently for the vacant head coaching job at Maryland, sources told NFL Network.","published":"2026-11-23T21:22:25.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/story/_/id/50575838/sources-giants-dennard-wilson-interviews-maryland-job","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"LSU's Lane Kiffin apologizes for using profanity during halftime interview","description":"LSU coach Lane Kiffin has apologized for using profanity during a halftime interview with the school's radio network in Saturday's loss to Tennessee.","published":"2026-11-23T20:12:55.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50575735/lsu-kiffin-apologizes-use-profanity-interview","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Mark Schlabach","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/4922989/jelani-mcdonald","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jelani_McDonald"},"pick":{"pick":40,"round":2,"team":"PHI","provisional":false},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Jelani McDonald","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jelani_McDonald","description":"American football player","touched":"2026-11-22T04:18:07Z","intro":"Jelani McDonald is an American college football safety for the Texas Longhorns.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"McDonald attended Connally High School in Waco, Texas, where he played both defensive back and quarterback. As a senior, he was the Offensive MVP of District 11-4A Division 2 after rushing 77 times for 852 yards with nine touchdowns, and passing for 707 yards with 13 touchdowns. On defense he had 25 tackles, four sacks and an interception. McDonald was selected to play in the 2023 All-American Bowl. He committed to play college football at the University of Texas at Austin."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"As a true freshman at Texas in 2023, McDonald played in 12 games and had two tackles. As a sophomore in 2024, he played in 14 games with four starts and recorded 33 tackles and one interception.\nMcDonald became a starting safety his junior year in 2025. In the first four weeks of the 2025 season, McDonald contributed to three turnovers in three consecutive games, logging one fumble recovery for 24 yards against San Jose State, one interception for 16 yards against UTEP, and one interception against Sam Houston. He ended the season with 80 tackles, three interceptions, and one fumble recovery.\nFor the 2026 season, McDonald chose to return for his senior year and continued as the starting safety. In Week 11 against LSU, McDonald recorded three interceptions, becoming the first SEC player to record three interceptions in a single game since 2020. For his performance, McDonald was named Player of the Week by the Associated Press, Chuck Bednarik Award,  Jim Thorpe Award, and Walter Camp Award."}]}}